<li>Navigate to the <a class="group inline" href="https://console.neon.tech" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Neon Console<span class="whitespace-nowrap no-underline"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="ml-1 inline-block size-3.5! shrink-0 align-[-0.125em]"><path fill="currentColor" d="M0 0h14v14H0z" opacity="0.2"></path><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" d="M9.915 8.885V4.08H5.11M9.625 4.375 4.083 9.917"></path></svg></span></a> to create a new Neon project.</li>
<li>Copy the connection string by clicking the <strong>Connect</strong> button on your <strong>Project Dashboard</strong>. For more information, see <a class="" href="/docs/connect/connect-from-any-app">Connect from any application</a>.</li>
</ol></div></li><li class="numbered-step relative mt-8! mb-0! flex w-full items-start gap-4 pl-0! before:flex before:size-7 before:items-center before:justify-center before:rounded-full before:bg-gray-new-20 before:text-center before:font-mono before:text-sm before:leading-snug before:font-medium before:tracking-tight before:text-white before:content-[counter(section)] before:[counter-increment:section] after:absolute after:top-8 after:-bottom-7 after:left-[.8125rem] after:w-px after:bg-gray-new-90 first:mt-0! last:after:bottom-0 dark:before:bg-gray-new-90 dark:before:text-black-pure dark:after:bg-gray-new-30 [&amp;_h2]:text-2xl [&amp;_ol]:list-decimal!"><div class="w-[calc(100%-100px)] flex-1 [&amp;&gt;*_*:last-child]:mb-0 [&amp;&gt;*:first-child]:mt-0 [&amp;&gt;*:first-child]:pt-0 md:[&amp;&gt;*:first-child]:mt-0 [&amp;&gt;*:last-child]:mb-0"><h2 id="create-an-aws-account-and-s3-bucket" class="anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-tighter"><span>Create an AWS account and S3 bucket</span><a class="rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden" href="#create-an-aws-account-and-s3-bucket" aria-label="Link to Create an AWS account and S3 bucket"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3.5"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.4" d="m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75"></path></svg></a></h2><ol>
<li>
<p>Sign up for or log in to your <a class="group inline" href="https://aws.amazon.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AWS Account<span class="whitespace-nowrap no-underline"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="ml-1 inline-block size-3.5! shrink-0 align-[-0.125em]"><path fill="currentColor" d="M0 0h14v14H0z" opacity="0.2"></path><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" d="M9.915 8.885V4.08H5.11M9.625 4.375 4.083 9.917"></path></svg></span></a>.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Navigate to the <strong>S3</strong> service in the AWS Management Console.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Click <strong>Create bucket</strong>. Provide a unique bucket name (for example, <code>my-neon-app-s3-uploads</code>), select an AWS Region (for example, <code>us-east-1</code>), and configure initial settings.
<span aria-owns="rmiz-modal-" data-rmiz=""><span data-rmiz-content="not-found" style="visibility:visible"><img alt="Create S3 Bucket" loading="lazy" width="704" height="447" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="" style="color:transparent;width:100%;height:100%" src="/docs/guides/aws-s3-create-bucket.png?dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7"/></span></span></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Public Access (for this example):</strong> For simplicity in accessing uploaded files via URL in this guide, we&#x27;ll configure the bucket to allow public read access <em>for objects uploaded with specific permissions</em>. Under <strong>Block Public Access settings for this bucket</strong>, <em>uncheck</em> &quot;Block all public access&quot;. Acknowledge the warning.
<span aria-owns="rmiz-modal-" data-rmiz=""><span data-rmiz-content="not-found" style="visibility:visible"><img alt="Public Access Settings" loading="lazy" width="704" height="447" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="" style="color:transparent;width:100%;height:100%" src="/docs/guides/aws-s3-public-access.png?dpl=dpl_3oQTwA9tDsjxX7vtodZE2SLAZ1X7"/></span></span></p>
<div class="admonition not-prose my-9 rounded-none border-l-2 bg-gray-new-98 py-4 pr-5 pl-[1.125rem] dark:bg-gray-new-8 border-[#2D8665] dark:border-green-52 [&amp;_pre]:px-4 [&amp;_pre]:py-3 [&amp;_pre_code]:text-sm! [&amp;_pre[data-language]]:bg-white! [&amp;_pre[data-language]]:dark:bg-gray-new-8!"><div class="flex items-center gap-1 text-[#2D8665] dark:text-green-52"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 16 16" class="shrink-0"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="m12 2 2 2-6.4 6.4-2.8.8.8-2.8z"></path><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M12.4 9.2v3.6a1.2 1.2 0 0 1-1.2 1.2h-8A1.2 1.2 0 0 1 2 12.8v-8a1.2 1.2 0 0 1 1.2-1.2h3.6"></path></svg><h4 class="font-mono text-[13px] leading-none font-medium -tracking-snug uppercase">Public buckets</h4></div><div class="admonition-text mt-2.5 text-base leading-normal tracking-extra-tight text-gray-new-20 dark:text-gray-new-85 [&amp;_a]:rounded-sm [&amp;_li]:text-base [&amp;_li]:leading-snug [&amp;_li]:tracking-extra-tight [&amp;_ul]:my-0 [&amp;_ol]:my-0"><p>Making buckets or objects publicly readable carries security risks. For production applications, it&#x27;s strongly recommended to:</p><ol>
<li>Keep buckets <strong>private</strong> (Block all public access enabled).</li>
<li>Use <strong>presigned URLs</strong> not only for uploads but also for <em>downloads</em> (temporary read access).
This guide uses public access for simplicity, but you should implement secure access controls in production.</li>
</ol></div></div>
</li>
<li>
