</blockquote></div></li><li class="numbered-step relative mt-8! mb-0! flex w-full items-start gap-4 pl-0! before:flex before:size-7 before:items-center before:justify-center before:rounded-full before:bg-gray-new-20 before:text-center before:font-mono before:text-sm before:leading-snug before:font-medium before:tracking-tight before:text-white before:content-[counter(section)] before:[counter-increment:section] after:absolute after:top-8 after:-bottom-7 after:left-[.8125rem] after:w-px after:bg-gray-new-90 first:mt-0! last:after:bottom-0 dark:before:bg-gray-new-90 dark:before:text-black-pure dark:after:bg-gray-new-30 [&amp;_h2]:text-2xl [&amp;_ol]:list-decimal!"><div class="w-[calc(100%-100px)] flex-1 [&amp;&gt;*_*:last-child]:mb-0 [&amp;&gt;*:first-child]:mt-0 [&amp;&gt;*:first-child]:pt-0 md:[&amp;&gt;*:first-child]:mt-0 [&amp;&gt;*:last-child]:mb-0"><h2 id="create-a-table-in-neon-for-file-metadata" class="anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-tighter"><span>Create a table in Neon for file metadata</span><a class="rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden" href="#create-a-table-in-neon-for-file-metadata" aria-label="Link to Create a table in Neon for file metadata"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3.5"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.4" d="m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75"></path></svg></a></h2><p>We need a table in Neon to store metadata about the objects uploaded to S3.</p><ol>
<li>
<p>Connect to your Neon database using the <a class="" href="/docs/get-started/query-with-neon-sql-editor">Neon SQL Editor</a> or a client like <a class="" href="/docs/connect/query-with-psql-editor">psql</a>. Create a table including the object key, URL, user ID, and timestamp:</p>
<figure class="code-block group/code-block relative flex flex-col [&amp;_pre]:min-w-full rounded-none border border-gray-new-80 dark:border-gray-new-20 [&amp;&gt;pre]:my-0 [&amp;&gt;pre]:rounded-none [&amp;&gt;pre]:bg-white! [&amp;&gt;pre]:py-4 [&amp;&gt;pre]:dark:bg-black-pure!" data-has-filename="false" data-line-numbers="false"><pre class="shiki css-variables" style="background-color:var(--shiki-background);color:var(--shiki-foreground)" tabindex="0" data-language="sql"><code class="grid"><span class="line" data-line="1"><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-keyword)">CREATE</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-keyword)"> TABLE</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-function)"> IF</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-keyword)"> NOT</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-token-keyword)"> EXISTS</span><span style="color:var(--shiki-foreground)"> s3_files (</span></span>
